                                            "Language unique to a particular group of people."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0328b6f-6a60-401d-9b1d-8ee8d72d4b48",
                                                "sense_id": "dac0444f-99b7-3db5-ada2-50ef123db144",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: jargon, argot, dialect, slang"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "abcd48c5-e53c-4de3-82a7-29ad2c6daba8",
                                                "sense_id": "dac0444f-99b7-3db5-ada2-50ef123db144",
                                                "text": "For those of a certain age, hiphop vernacular might just as well be a foreign language."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f3d8b86d-e2e2-33ac-ab3e-716baeff234c",
                                        "entry_id": "2563396e-3292-30c2-99a4-bdc83d517636",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A language lacking standardization or a written form."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "844a7d70-10ad-3388-b3c3-4fd95500eafc",
                                        "entry_id": "2563396e-3292-30c2-99a4-bdc83d517636",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Indigenous spoken language, as distinct from a literary or liturgical language such as Ecclesiastical Latin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c318e76-639e-4f53-874a-eeb886675ed6",
                                                "sense_id": "844a7d70-10ad-3388-b3c3-4fd95500eafc",
                                                "text": "Vatican II, a church council in the 1960s, allowed the celebration of the mass in the vernacular."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
