                                            "A style of architecture involving local building materials and styles; not imported."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "vernacular",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6d2dd078-ec69-30b3-9101-346544e53770",
                                        "entry_id": "a5032d49-2283-3750-95a4-d33f5092a1be",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to everyday language, as opposed to standard, literary, liturgical, or scientific idiom."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "457b4dab-c199-4217-bc16-ddad1e66aeb1",
                                                "sense_id": "6d2dd078-ec69-30b3-9101-346544e53770",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: common, everyday, indigenous, ordinary, vulgar, colloquial, basilectal, demotic"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "adb0a3cd-ed24-44e5-92be-a879d424f74d",
                                                "sense_id": "6d2dd078-ec69-30b3-9101-346544e53770",
                                                "text": "There are blacktips, silvertips, bronze whalers, black whalers, spinner sharks, and bignose sharks. These of course are vernacular names, but this is one case where the scientific nomenclature does not clarify the species, since it is now being revised."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8af322f4-3f0f-3cc1-a28c-99f99314d860",
                                        "entry_id": "a5032d49-2283-3750-95a4-d33f5092a1be",
